</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate LoRAN on two representative NLP tasks: the SAMSum dialogue summarization dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> and the 20 Newsgroups classification task <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>. We use four foundation models—Flan-T5-Large <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>, Falcon-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, LLaMA-2-7B, and LLaMA-2-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>—to cover a spectrum of model sizes and architectures. Unless otherwise specified, we adopt QLoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> as the base PEFT implementation, with a LoRA rank of 64 and a scaling factor of 16. All models are fine-tuned for 5 epochs using AdamW with learning rate <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size 16. LoRAN is implemented by appending a non-linear transformation after the low-rank LoRA updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are run on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU (40GB). Our proposed Sinter activation is configured with <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, determined by a grid search described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="IV-D Robustness of LoRAN ‣ IV Experiments ‣ Enhancing Low-Rank Adaptation with Structured Nonlinear Transformations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
