LoRAN method on the SAMSum task. The foundation model is Llama-2-7b.<sup id="S4.T4.9.1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup><sup id="S4.T4.9.2" class="ltx_sup">‡</sup>Swish-1 and Swish-25 refer to
apply <math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> = 1 and <math id="S4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> = 25 in the Swish function. <span id="S4.T4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">78.24</span> indicates the best performance, and <span id="S4.T4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">77.78</span> indicates the second best.</span></figcaption>
