<td id="S5.T10.3.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">talk.religion.misc (#18)</td>
<td id="S5.T10.3.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">338</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T10.3.21" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.3.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">alt.atheism (#19)</td>
<td id="S5.T10.3.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">448</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T10.3.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.3.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">soc.religion.christian (#20)</td>
<td id="S5.T10.3.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">581</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>: </span><span id="S5.T10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Broad and fine-grained categories in the 20 newsgroups
task. Each fine-grained category corresponds to a
specific topic, while similar topics are clustered
into a broad category.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Limitations</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While LoRAN demonstrates consistent improvements over existing PEFT methods, two major limitations remain. First, although Sinter is lightweight, its periodic nature may introduce mild training instabilities in large-scale models under certain conditions. Second, While LoRAN introduces no additional parameters, the non-linear transformation does incur a modest increase in computational time. In our experiments with LLaMA-2 (7B and 13B), this overhead remains minimal—under 0.5 GPU hours (see Table <a href="#S5.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ V Conclusion and Future Work ‣ Enhancing Low-Rank Adaptation with Structured Nonlinear Transformations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Furthermore, such cost can be further reduced with kernel fusion or operator-level optimization techniques.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VII </span><span id="S7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Acknowledgements</span></h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work was supported in part by the Research Grants Council of the Hong Kong SAR under Grant GRF 11217823, Grant GRF 11216225 and Collaborative Research Fund C1042-23GF, the National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant 62371411, InnoHK initiative, the Government of the HKSAR, Laboratory for AI-Powered Financial Technologies.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">[20 Newsgroups Task]</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ V Conclusion and Future Work ‣ Enhancing Low-Rank Adaptation with Structured Nonlinear Transformations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, the 20 classes correspond to fine-grained news topics, which are further grouped into five broader categories based on semantic similarity. The table also details the number of samples per class.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A0.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ VII Acknowledgements ‣ Enhancing Low-Rank Adaptation with Structured Nonlinear Transformations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> illustrates the performance improvement of LoRAN over QLoRA for each class. For fine-grained categories (marked in red), a correct prediction requires an exact match with the gold label. In contrast, for broad categories (marked in blue), a prediction is considered correct if it falls within the correct broader group.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p5.1" class="ltx_p">When the rank is high (<math id="S7.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=64</annotation></semantics></math>), LoRAN’s performance gains primarily arise from fine-grained categories, as it can leverage sufficient parameters to fit more nuanced patterns. Conversely, at a lower rank (<math id="S7.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=8</annotation></semantics></math>), improvements are mostly seen in broad categories, which are easier to predict and require less representational capacity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This pattern reflects the relative difficulty of the tasks: distinguishing broad categories is generally easier than identifying specific fine-grained classes. With <math id="S7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=64</annotation></semantics></math>, LoRA can already achieve high accuracy on broad categories, leaving room for LoRAN to improve upon the harder fine-grained ones through its non-linear transformation mechanism. However, when the rank drops to <math id="S7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=8</annotation></semantics></math>, LoRA’s linear adapter lacks the capacity to reliably separate even broad categories. In such cases, LoRAN’s non-linearity shifts focus toward the simpler task—broad category prediction—resulting in greater gains in those classes, as reflected in Figure <a href="#A0.F6.sf2" title="In Fig. 6 ‣ VII Acknowledgements ‣ Enhancing Low-Rank Adaptation with Structured Nonlinear Transformations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6(b)</span></a>. This demonstrates that LoRAN can enhance LoRA’s performance even under constrained settings such as low-rank configurations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A0.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A0.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.21870v1/figures/newsgroups_rank64.png" id="A0.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/210;" width="476" height="210" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F6.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A0.F6.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=64</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A0.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.21870v1/figures/newsgroups_rank8.png" id="A0.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/235;" width="476" height="235" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F6.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><math id="A0.F6.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=8</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 6</span>: </span><span id="A0.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Topic-level classification accuracy of QLoRA and LoRAN on the 20 Newsgroups task. The foundation model is Llama-2-7b.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
